    "body": "## Summary\n\nTileLang SparseMLA was mapped but treated as dense full-context MLA (`g_sk≈1.75e6` → ~1815 MiB / ~87 TB/s). Cap generation KV to indexer topk from `Input Dims[2][-1]` via existing `sliding_window` / `_cap_gen_kv`, matching SGLang `tilelang_sparse_fwd` (`topk = indices.shape[-1]`):\n\nhttps://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/b498f462/python/sglang/kernels/ops/attention/dsa/tilelang_kernel.py#L1310-L1322\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Unit test: glm53 dims, capped `g_sk`, bytes ≪ 1815 MiB, BW ≪ 7.4 TB/s\n- [x] Fail-closed when indices dims missing\n- [ ] Smoke: glm53 decode report with `--capture_folder` → `TB/s_mean` order ~1 TB/s, `has_perf_model=True`\n\n## Follow-up (out of scope)\n\nCharge one MLA latent read (576-d) instead of separate K+V; optionally index-byte term.",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": null,
